<title>UK: Cypriot freighter finally refloated at Veracruz.</title>
<headline>Cypriot freighter finally refloated at Veracruz.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cyprus-flag freighter Nika II was refloated on March 8 at Veracruz, Mexico and has been towed to anchorage, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The 15,251 dwt vessel ran aground last month but efforts to refloat the ship to date have been hampered by bad weather.</p>
<p>The Nika II sailed from Abidjan on January 23 and was inbound to Veracruz to load a cargo of bagged sugar for Algeria.</p>
</text>
